s","Utilities"],"rows":[],"meta":{"what":"Aggregate FPI/FII stake per listed company, from the quarterly shareholding filing","source":"Screener-cached shareholding tables (data/screener/*.json); market cap from legacy_mcap_daily.csv","grain":"one row per (symbol, calendar quarter-end)","signal":"d_fii_pp = quarter-on-quarter change in FII % of equity, in PERCENTAGE POINTS. Price-neutral by construction (a % of the company cannot be moved by price alone), so it needs no de-pricing \u2014 the foreign analogue of weight-space net-active.","value_identity":"H = f*M ; dH = f_prev*dM (value effect) + M_now*df (flow effect); residual 1.02e-10 cr","n_symbols":2883,"n_symbol_quarters":32109,"n_steps":29036,"n_linked_vid":2829,"n_linked_sector":1558,"caveats":["QUARTERLY and LAGGED \u2014 filings land ~3-6 weeks after quarter end; never read as timely.","SHORT HISTORY \u2014 44 quarters only. Descriptive positioning context, NOT a validated signal; it would likely fail a strict signal_navtest bar.","SHARE ISSUANCE moves FII% mechanically: a QIP/rights/ESOP that FPIs skip dilutes their stake without any selling, and a buyback lifts it. mcap_jump marks the suspect quarters.","'FIIs' can include strategic/FDI-type foreign holders, not only portfolio money.","NOT attributable to any named manager \u2014 India publishes no 13F. Names only appear above 1% (module B1) and above 5% (SAST, already in events.py).","Rupee views cover only the ~800 names with market-cap history; the % panel is wider."]}}